## Context

Step A of the 0978 relocation, sequenced in controlled-risk steps (author, 2026-09-29).
Create `~/.idh -> ~/.claude` and repoint every live consumer to `~/.idh` (or `$IDH_ROOT`)
while the bytes stay where they are. Both paths resolve to the same files, so nothing can
break and no quiet window is needed; the later cutover (0986) then becomes local.

Census 2026-09-29: 263 of 2,171 tracked files name `~/.claude` literally (mostly tickets and
memory prose). Live wiring in the repo: `settings.shared.json`, `adapters/codex/hooks.json`,
`adapters/pilot-support.json`, `scripts/bash-env.sh`, `scripts/on-start.sh`,
`scripts/projects.json`, `scripts/adapter-claude-code-activate.sh`,
`scripts/check-primary-checkout.sh`, `scripts/check-agnostic.sh`, `bin/`, `skills/`, `tests/`.
Outside the repo: `~/.bashrc:159` (shell-init), systemd user units `claude-refresh`,
`cadens-harvest`, `claude-telemetry-prune`, `~/.codex/config.toml`, `~/.codex/hooks.json`,
`~/.pi/agent/settings.json`, `aedist/.claude/settings.local.json`, and padme (unchecked).

Out of scope: paths that are Claude Code's native root on purpose (`~/.claude/projects/`,
`~/.claude/settings.json` as the runtime reads it) stay spelled `~/.claude`, with a reason.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `~/.idh` exists as a pointer to the current checkout; installation documented
- [ ] Every live consumer in and out of the repo names `~/.idh` or `$IDH_ROOT`; the out-of-repo list above is recorded with per-item evidence (padme included)
- [ ] A ratchet test fails on a new literal `~/.claude/` in scripts, hooks, adapters or settings outside an allowlist of native-root paths; its positive control fires on a planted literal
- [ ] A fresh Claude, Codex and Pi session each load hooks and instructions as before
- [ ] `make check` passes
